.TH CANDLED.CONF 5 "November 2026" "wincan" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
candled.conf \- configuration file of candled
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR candled (8)
reads its settings from this file, by default
.I /etc/candled.conf
(the system configuration directory it was built with) if there is one, or the file named with
.BR \-\-config .
An option of the command line overrides the file; a setting that neither gives has the default below.
.PP
The notation is that of
.BR obconf :
a directive is a keyword and its argument, ended by the end of the line.  A string is in double quotes (it must be, if it has a space; file names may also be written bare), with C's backslash escapes; a backslash at the end of a line continues it.
.B #
starts a comment that runs to the end of the line.  There are no includes, macros or conditions.  A directive may be given once (a later one replaces an earlier one), except
.BR authorize ,
which may be repeated.  A file with an error is not used: every error is printed as
.IR file:line: message
and candled does not start (\fB\-\-check\-config\fR tells whether a file is good).
.PP
The parser was generated by the hbnf parser generator meta compiler (https://github.com/moebiusV/hbnf) from
.I grammars/candled.hbnf
in the source.
.SH DIRECTIVES
.TP
.BI listen " ADDRESS"
the IPv4 address to listen on, or
.B *
for all of them.  Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 ,
the loopback address: only this computer (and, with candled in WSL2, the Windows it runs in) can connect.
.TP
.BI port " N"
the TCP port, 1 to 65535.  Default 8766.
.TP
.BI tls " yes" | no
whether connections are encrypted and a client must show an authorized key.  Default
.BR yes .
.TP
.BI insecure " yes" | no
allow plain HTTP (\fBtls no\fR) on an address that is not a loopback address.  Without it candled refuses to start in that case.  Default
.BR no .
.TP
.BI certificate " FILE"
.TQ
.BI key " FILE"
the server's certificate and private key, PEM; made by
.BR "candled \-\-gen\-cert" .
Default
.I /etc/candled/server.crt
and
.IR /etc/candled/server.key .
.TP
.BI authorized " FILE"
the file of the fingerprints of the clients that are let in; one on a line, with notes after a
.BR # .
Default
.IR /etc/candled/authorized\-clients .
.TP
.BI authorize " SHA256:HEX"
a client let in by the file itself: the SHA\-256 fingerprint of its certificate, \fBSHA256:\fR and 64 hexadecimal digits.  May be repeated.
.TP
.BI candles " DIR"
the directory of the collector's NAME.bin files.  Default
.I /var/lib/candled/candles
(the state directory it was built with).
.TP
.BI backfill " DIR"
a second directory of .bin files, for the time before the first has data.
.TP
.BI database " FILE"
a SQLite database of one\-minute candles (a table
.BR candles ).
.TP
.BI live\-bins " DIR"
a websocket daemon's directory of one\-minute candles.
.TP
.BI heat\-db " FILE"
the liquidation\-map database for wincan's heat strip (see
.BR candled (8),
HEAT DATABASE).
.TP
.BI official\-klines " yes" | no
fetch the exchange's own candles of the last minutes, and the mark price.  Default
.BR no .
.PP
The meaning of each is that of the option of the same name in
.BR candled (8).
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
# a candle server for this computer and the Windows it runs in
listen 127.0.0.1
port 8766
candles "/var/lib/candled/candles"
database "/var/lib/candled/candles.db"
authorize "SHA256:0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"  # the desktop
.fi
.SH FILES
.I /etc/candled.conf
.br
.I /usr/share/doc/wincan/examples/candled.conf.sample
(a commented sample; the installed one is a copy of it)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR candled (8),
.BR candle\-protocol (7),
.BR wincan (5)
